        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9092381?u=fde5fbface3f55bc6d96ff4c5701637f9a01bf0f&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Unlike the wait methods, <code class=\"notranslate\">Atomics.notify()</code> does not throw when passed a view on a non-shared array buffer. The MDN documentation mostly alludes to this behaviour correctly, but incorrectly states that it will throw a <code class=\"notranslate\">TypeError</code> if passed such an argument.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-atomics.notify\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-atomics.notify</a></p>",
